SOURCE IMAGERY
--------------
Derived from Mastcam multispectral imagery acquired by the Mars Science
Laboratory (Curiosity) rover and archived by the NASA Planetary Data System
(PDS) Imaging Node. Original data courtesy NASA/JPL-Caltech/MSSS.

CHANGES MADE, as CC-BY requires be indicated
--------------------------------------------
1. Frames converted from float64 .npy to memory-mapped float32 arrays
   (scripts/preprocess.py). No resampling; a dtype narrowing only.
2. Splits materialised as test_novel_all (430 unique frames) and
   test_novel_byclass (451 frame-label pairs) to stop the archive's overlapping
   all/ and per-class folders being double-counted. See the README section
   "The test_novel gotcha".
3. Thumbnails rendered for display in web/public/data/atlas.png: three of the
   six bands mapped to RGB with fixed per-channel gains and a per-frame
   contrast stretch, downsampled 64x64 -> 32x32 by exact box average. The
   mapping is documented in core/thumbnails.py. These are a VISUALISATION and
   not a calibrated radiometric product; no measurement in this project is
   made on them.

WHAT IS AND IS NOT REDISTRIBUTED HERE
-------------------------------------
No raw or processed dataset frames are committed to this repository; data/ is
gitignored and fetched from Zenodo by scripts/fetch_data.py. The rendered
thumbnail atlas IS committed, as a derived work under the same CC-BY-4.0 terms,
with the attribution above reproduced in the console UI.
